"sha256":"6c760d36b1d22350dc22890bbf31afb0a67911c3bc295abd567cc0e706fe2ccd","url":"https://hdl.handle.net/2027/uiug.30112026470077"}},"suggested":false}],"whole_order_end_total":2},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"confirm","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1981-01-19","later-events_catalog":"1981-01-19","stage19_causal_queue":"1981-01-19"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:12285","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-101. There is established the President’s Commission on Hostage Compensa­\ntion, hereinafter referred to as the Commission, which shall be composed of  \nnot more than nine members who shall be appointed by the President.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-101","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-101","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-102. The President shall designate a Chairman from among the members.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-102","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-102","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-201. The Commission shall study and analyze, and make recommendations  \nto the President on, the question whether the United States should provide  \nfinancial compensation to United States nationals who have been held in  \ncaptivity outside the United States, either (1) by or with the approval of a  \nforeign government, or (2) by reason of their status as employees of the United  \nStates Government or as dependents of such employees.\n1— 202. The Commission shall submit a report to the President ninety days after  \nthe date of this Order. The report shall contain the Commission’s recommen­\ndations as to whether legislation to deal with the foregoing com pensation  \nissue is appropriate and, if so, as to w hat such legislation should provide. The  \nreport shall specifically contain the Commission’s recommendations concern­\ning the compensation of United States nationals held hostage in Iran on and  \nafter November 4,1979.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-201","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-201","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-203. In analyzing the foregoing issues the Commission shall consider all  \nfactors which it m ay consider relevant, including the prior practice with  \nrespect to governmental compensation, both by the United States Government  \nand by foreign governments, of persons held in captivity abroad.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-203","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-203","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-204. In the performance of its functions the Commission shall specifically  \naddress the following issues:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-204 (lead-in)","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-204","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) whether any legislation authorizing compensation should set forth specific  \nlegislative standards, or whether the standards by which to aw ard com pensa­\ntion should be administratively developed;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-204(a)","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-204(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) whether any standards developed either legislatively or administratively  \nshould be applied uniformly to civilian and military government employees,  \ndependents of such employees, and private citizens, or whether separate  \ncriteria should be developed for these or other categories;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-204(b)","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-204(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) whether an existing administrative body should determine amounts of  \ncompensation, or whether a new body should be established for this purpose;  \nand\n(d) whether compensation should be paid for injuries suffered by members of  \nfamilies of persons who have been held in captivity.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-204(c)","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-204(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-3. A d m in is t r a t iv e  P r o v is io n s .","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-3","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-301. In performing its functions the Commission shall conduct such studies,  \nreviews, and inquiries as m ay be necessary. In addition to conducting open  \nmeetings in accordance with the Federal Advisory Committee Act, the Com-\n\n=== PDF page 698 of 700 ===\n7932 Federal Register /  Vol. 46, No. 15 /  Friday, January 23,1981 /  Presidential Documents\nmission shall conduct public hearings to identify critical issues and possible  \nsolutions related to compensation.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-301","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-301","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-302. The Commission is authorized to request from any Executive agency  \nsuch information that m ay be deemed necessary to carry out its functions  \nunder this Order. Each Executive agency shall, to the extent permitted by law,  \nfurnish such information to the Commission in the performance of its functions  \nunder this Order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-302","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-302","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-303. Each member of the Commission who is not otherwise employed in the  \nFederal Government m ay receive, to the extent permitted by law, compensa­\ntion for each day he or she is engaged in the work of the Commission at a rate  \nnot to exceed the maximum daily rate now or hereafter prescribed by law for  \nG S-18 of the General Schedule, and m ay also receive trànsportation and  \ntravel expenses, including per diem in lieu of subsistence, as authorized by  \nlaw  (5 U.S.C. 5702 and 5703).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-303","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-303","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-304. All necessary administrative staff services, support, facilities, and  \nexpenses of the Commission shall, to the extent permitted by law, be fur­\nnished by the Department of State.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-304","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-304","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-4. G e n e r a l P r o v is io n s .","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-4","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-401. Notwithstanding the provisions of any other Executive Order, the  \nfunctions of the President under the Federal Advisory Committee Act, as  \namended (5 U.S.C. App. I), except that of reporting annually to the Congress,  \nwhich are applicable to the Commission, shall be performed by the Secretary  \nof State in accordance with guidelines and procedures established by the  \nAdministrator of General Services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-401","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-401","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-402. The Commission shall terminate thirty days after submitting its report.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698; Sec. 1-402","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12285#sec1-402","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"46 FR 7931, PDF pages 697-698","sha256":"52a382016c007eb78e1209194fdc49a3f40dc79b8512fce9bf08ee54852d63db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1981-01-23/pdf/FR-1981-01-23.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 16 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12285"}
